---
description: Scientific integrity for AI-generated research artifacts
alwaysApply: true
---

Integrity beats fluency.

- Every numeric claim in a manuscript must appear in `execution.log` or be marked `[UNVERIFIED]`.
- Do not optimize an LLM reviewer score alone. That is the Chen 2025 / AI-Scientist failure mode.
- If the experiment failed, report the failure. Do not invent a table.
- Plagiarism check n-grams against the SOTA catalog and any pasted papers before a draft is "done".
- Related Work must distinguish ancestry (Coscientist 2023, AI Scientist 2024) from this week's result.
- A survey is not a discovery. A held-out metric plus logs is.
